  "id": "COMPOUND:3194 - PROTEIN:2468",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between alpha-D-Xylopyranose and Pulmonary surfactant-associated protein D, mediated through Beta-D-Glucose. This is supported by two distinct pathways: one where alpha-D-Xylopyranose directly targets Endoglucanase E1, which in turn is targeted by Beta-D-Glucose, and another where alpha-D-Xylopyranose targets Putrescine-binding periplasmic protein, which is also targeted by Beta-D-Glucose. Both pathways ultimately lead to the same target, Pulmonary surfactant-associated protein D. The shared involvement of Beta-D-Glucose in both pathways implies a possible functional overlap or regulatory mechanism, potentially linking alpha-D-Xylopyranose to the protein through a common intermediate. The evidence suggests that alpha-D-Xylopyranose may influence the activity of Beta-D-Glucose, which then modulates Pulmonary surfactant-associated protein D, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
